"""Source-bound recovery amendments. Original unpublished draft is immutable elsewhere."""
from pathlib import Path
import json,hashlib
B=Path(__file__).parent/'B02m'
def read(n):return json.loads((B/n).read_text())
def write(n,v):(B/n).write_text(json.dumps(v,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\n')
def digest(v):return hashlib.sha256(json.dumps(v,sort_keys=True,ensure_ascii=False,separators=(',',':')).encode()).hexdigest()
D=read('RULES.json'); OLD={r['id']:json.loads(json.dumps(r)) for r in D['rules']}; R={int(r['id'].rsplit('R',1)[1]):r for r in D['rules']}
# These are normalized documentary paraphrases, not instructions to treat any person.
DETAIL={
1651:['The heading names Hermes Trismegistus and the first decumbiture. Planetary rays are said to disperse into human members as conception first forms in the womb, and again at birth. The head is assigned Aries according to the twelve signs.'],
1652:['Right eye: Sun. Left eye: Moon. Hearing and ears: Saturn. Brain: Jupiter. Blood: Mars. Smelling and tasting: Venus. Tongue and the printed weesell-pipe of the throat or lung-pipe: Mercury. No sex-dependent eye reversal appears in this local table.'],
1653:['A member is said to suffer a defect or imperfection when an afflicted planet had dominion over it or signified it at conception or birth. The alternative times and dominion/signification are retained.'],
1654:['Four additional principal/general parts are named: head, breast, hands and feet. An unfortunate or ill-affected governing planet at conception or birth is said to afflict or disfigure all its assigned parts, or a particular/principal part of those members.'],
1655:['Ill-disposed Sun, Moon, or both injure the eyes; Saturn the ears, teeth or hearing; oppressed Mercury the tongue or speech, including stammering. The text extends the same manner of inquiry to breast, lungs, liver, spleen, heart and intestinal/inward parts, without supplying a complete new planet-to-organ table.','For hands and feet, fingers and nails are inspected for imperfection attributed to a predominating malignant planet. These are illustrations and attributed mechanisms, not identified patient outcomes.'],
1656:['For defects within the compass of cure, the author advocates convenient medicines and resistance to an afflicting planet by planets of contrary nature and power. The curability restriction is part of the source.'],
1657:['Saturn is assigned medicaments described as cooling or refrigerating and extenuating with dryness and siccity. This is a class assignment, not the instruction to treat Saturn-caused illness with Saturn-like medicines.'],
1658:['Mercury is assigned substances described as congealing, flatulent and windy.'],
1659:['Mars is assigned calefactive, warm and impletive substances, as a very sharp heater and procurator of blood in the source rhetoric.'],
1660:['Jupiter and Venus are both assigned conglutinating and mollifying things, described as effective to assuage and cure all ulcers. The strong efficacy wording is preserved as an author assertion, not endorsed evidence.'],
1661:['The Moon helps or lends assistance to the planet to which she applies, whether it is good or bad. Assistance is not itself a favourable patient outcome.'],
1662:['For a sick or lame person the source requests a figure for the hour of first falling sick or lying down, with the planets, their dispositions and mutual relations considered.','It also asserts that no worldly affair is firm without these influences and no physician, however learned, can cure without a benevolent stellar configuration: absent it the patient perishes, or through kind influences recovers. This necessity claim is doctrinal rhetoric, not an empirical result.'],
1663:['If the certain first-illness hour cannot be known precisely, use the time when judgment is required of the physician. This is a fallback, not permission to choose whichever chart gives a preferred result.'],
1664:['Inspect the planet from which the Moon separates, the one to which she applies, and her square, opposition or conjunction. Configuration with malefics is said to extend the illness almost to death; with fortunes, remedy comes more speedily. Almost to death is not an unconditional death prediction.'],
1665:['Observe whether the Moon is swift in motion and increasing in light, whether both happen at once, or neither. The two properties are not interchangeable; no numerical speed threshold is printed here.'],
1666:['After conjunction with the Sun, the Moon grows in light and motion. If she is afflicted by Mars square or opposition before reaching opposition to the Sun, with no intervening aspect of a benevolent planet, the text assigns mortal and pernicious diseases. All sequential and exclusion conditions belong together.'],
1667:['If the Moon is conjoined with, or in good aspect to, beneficial stars, the infirm body is said to recover even when the sick person was absolutely persuaded of non-survival. This preserves the source certainty as a claim, not a calibrated probability.'],
1668:['The Moon decreasing in light AND motion and afflicted by Saturn square OR opposition is said to signify an incurable, mortal disease, UNLESS its vigour remits presently after opposition to Saturn.','Application to benevolent planets is separately said to bring a speedy cure. The remission exception specifically names the opposition, not any Saturn contact. Decreasing motion is not automatically identical to merely being below a mean speed.'],
1669:['At the first onset the text associates increasing Moon in number and light with increasing disease; when the Moon grows slow in motion, sickness diminishes. Number remains an undefined source term. This general statement must not silently override other local compound rules.'],
1670:['At first lying down under malignant Saturn OR Mercury, the source describes heaviness, drowsiness, unwilling movement of diseased members, stupor or numbness with excessive cold, and unnatural defluxions. Illness steals on gradually and the person is not easily awakened even when urged.','Further descriptions: silence in speech, fearfulness, desire for hot plasters or fomentations, preference for darkness, constant sighing, gently drawing or sucking in breath, short wind, a swift and painful pulse, comfort from warmth, feeble pulses, and a cold/dry bodily exterior. Both pulse descriptions are retained without reconciliation.','The proposed remedies are naturally hot, mollifying and constringing. They are documented as historical claims only.'],
1671:['Adverse Sun OR Mars configurations at first illness are associated with disturbed mind and fancy, difficult or rugged demeanour, inflamed superficial parts, anger, clamour/noise, peevish looks, staring, thirst and a rough parched tongue.','Other descriptions: desire for wine, cold drink and baths; no food sharpens appetite; abusive language; short, depressed and inordinate pulse; red faces and bodily fullness.','The historical prescription mentions letting blood until the fifth day, medicines evacuating or purging bodily foulness, and further remedies as nature requires. No modern recommendation or dose follows from this preservation.'],
1672:['Mars-compatible medicines are described as calefactive, emollient/mollifying and dissolving obstructions, repugnant to Saturn; Saturn-compatible substances as refrigerating/cooling, astringent/binding and repercussing, contrary to Mars.','Infirmities, passions and trembling of the heart, those from the mouth of the stomach, and pains of arteries, veins and joints are attributed to evil Mars and Sun influence.','Continued fevers, phrensies, exulceration and inflammation of lungs/lights are then attributed to Saturn and Mercury, with refrigerating medicines called most proper. This explicit target-and-remedy statement differs from the heating/softening recommendation for Saturn/Mercury origins on PDF307 (R1675). Preserve the local tension; do not silently swap planets or a remedy polarity.'],
1673:['The cooling list occupies three columns on PDF306. Its individual source lexemes and uncertainties are in MATERIA_MEDICA_TABLES.json; it is not a list of verified effective or safe modern medicines.'],
1674:['The heating list is assigned to Mars and Sun and spans PDF306–307. Three columns continue across the page turn; the individual source lexemes and uncertain identities are in MATERIA_MEDICA_TABLES.json.'],
1675:['For disease origins attributed to Saturn OR Mercury, to be discovered from the Moon course, the text prescribes naturally heating and mollifying substances. For Solar and Martial diseases it prescribes refrigerative, cooling and repercussive remedies. This does not erase the differently worded prescription in R1672.'],
1676:['The heading concerns signs and conjectures of disease, life or death from the Moon at the patient first lying down or demanding the question.','The Saturn catalogue introduction specifies decreasing lunar light AND motion, a Moon in one of twelve signs, and Saturn square, opposition OR conjunction. The person is said to share some or all of the listed diseases during the illness; the alternatives are not a requirement that every symptom be present.'],
1677:['Inherited Saturn-catalogue conditions plus Moon in Aries. Symptoms: headache or head heaviness; rheum in nostrils; singing ears; snuffing in the head; weary/dull eyes; rheum and corrupt humours descending into throat and windpipe; weak, inordinate pulses; drowsy mind; stomach loathing; intemperate/unseasonable sweats; heat within and cold without; worse by night than day.','If the Moon receives no favourable aspect of a good planet, the source asserts death, God sending no extraordinary remedy. Both lack of assistance and the extraordinary-remedy clause remain explicit.','Loosening the belly is described as relieving the grief, while letting blood is called ill in this row. These local historical prescriptions are not clinical instructions.'],
1678:['Inherited Saturn-catalogue conditions plus Moon in Taurus. Fevers proceed from obstructions/distemper of the praecordiacks and arteries, glossed as inward parts near heart, liver and lungs; excess, surfeits or repletion are alleged causes. High/lofty but immoderate pulses, bodily puffing and lung ulceration are described.','Without gentle fortunate aspects to the Moon the party will hardly live fourteen days; under a good aspect the sick may recover beyond expectation. The latter is possibility, not certainty. Purging/dissolving gross humours and phlebotomy are described as good in this row.'],
1679:['Inherited Saturn-catalogue conditions plus Moon in Gemini. Alleged causes: mental weariness and overburden from many affairs, travel, excessive bodily exercise. Small-fever fear and pain dispersed through the body, especially arteries/joints.','A first-person passage reports afflicted vitals, tendency to consumption, rare/little pulse, frequent sweat, spleen symptoms, and worse illness at night.','If Mars TOGETHER WITH Saturn afflicts the Moon at the same time, most authors are reported to hold that the sick will not live above ten days, UNLESS a favourable Jupiter OR Venus aspect intervenes; then after a long time the sick MAY recover. This is attributed testimony, not a counted patient series.'],
1680:['Inherited Saturn-catalogue conditions plus Moon in Cancer. Breast affected by tough melancholy matter or slimy thick phlegm; coughs, abundant spittle/moisture, catarrhs, hoarseness, rheum descending into breast, narrow obstructed pipes, small fevers, fear of quotidian but usually a long quartan ague; belly ache or infirmity in reins/secrets.','If the Moon is decreasing and near Saturn body, the sickness continues a great space of time. In a further clause, if together with lunar affliction the ascendant lord is impeded by the eighth lord, there are small hopes of recovery. The proximity-duration and additional ruler-impediment clauses are distinct; do not turn small hopes into certain death.'],
1681:['Inherited Saturn-catalogue conditions plus Moon in Leo. Melancholy blood, unkindly breast heat, strained heartstrings, violent fevers/troubled pulse, harmful inner/outer heat, sometimes stone, heart faintness or swooning. Black jaundice is a danger IF the illness continues long.','The source proposes gentle moistening/heating. When the Moon reaches opposition to Saturn, if Jupiter OR Venus does not assist by sextile, trine OR conjunction, the sick dies many times. The frequency phrase and specified assisting aspects are retained.'],
1682:['Inherited Saturn-catalogue conditions plus Moon in Virgo. Crudities/ill digestion in stomach, viscous phlegm obstructing bowels/intrails, shooting/pricking under ribs and inordinate fevers.','First-person additions: wind-colic, extreme melancholy, gout or aches in thighs/feet. Mollifying, heating and dissolving things are called proper. The author seldom finds such illness anything but long, giving earthy Virgo and slow Saturn as rationale; not a measured duration or independent causal demonstration.'],
1683:['Inherited Saturn-catalogue conditions plus Moon in Libra. Alleged origins are excess wine, gluttony, undigested food or too much venery. Breast/head affected, absent appetite and stomach loathing, cough, hoarseness and rheum.','First-person continuation across PDF309–310: great pains in joints, knees and thighs, with itch in those parts and fear of sciatica. These observations share the same row, not separate patients.'],
1684:['Inherited Saturn-catalogue conditions plus Moon in Scorpio. Anal ulcer, haemorrhoids/piles, exulceration, bubo or a blotch in private members are described.','The first-person enquiry passage explicitly reads no retention of Urine; also bladder stone, swelling dropsical humour around knees/legs, sometimes flux; for a man gonorrhea, for a woman abundant menstrual discharge. No retention must not be normalized to retention. Modern diagnosis or urinary subtype is not inferred.'],
1685:['Inherited Saturn-catalogue conditions plus Moon in Sagittarius. Thin/sharp defluxions, arteries/joints pain, fear of fever, extremes of heat/cold and often double fever access. Gently mitigating heat and moistening is the local historical prescription.','First-person conjunction with Saturn: infected choleric/melancholy blood, sometimes excessive pains-taking or violent exercise followed by cold. Opposition to Saturn: for the most part gout or tumour/swelling in hands, thighs or feet.','Mars ALSO casting an ill aspect to the Moon, as well as Saturn, at first falling sick is required for the subsequent violent burning-fever assertion.'],
1686:['Inherited Saturn-catalogue conditions plus Moon in Capricorn. Cold/melancholy, thin subtle distillations, heaviness of breast/stomach, difficult breathing, dry cough, oppressed lungs, inward fever, more pain at night. Moderate heating/moistening is the source remedy.','The first-person continuation across PDF310–311 adds headache, pain in the LEFT ear, or rumbling/noise in the head.'],
1687:['Inherited Saturn-catalogue conditions plus Moon in Aquarius. Too much labour/toil of body and mind, lack of sleep and due refreshment are alleged origins. Illness is uneven, remitting and intensifying, until the Moon passes opposition to HER OWN INITIAL PLACE; if fortunes then have a good aspect to her, the sick is recoverable.','First-person additions: wind or noise in the head; faint fits/passions of heart; often sore throat or a rising there and danger of suffocation. No fixed day count is supplied for the geometrical event.'],
1688:['Inherited Saturn-catalogue conditions plus Moon in Pisces. Cold distillations, continual fevers and sighing, pricking/shooting under the paps, extensions of praecordiacks and heartstrings.','First-person additions: excess cold, throat oppressed with thick phlegm, breast troubled by rotten cough and watery matter. Heating and gently calisfying medicines are described as good; no temperature, dose or modern drug is supplied.'],
1689:['The transition describes the completed twelve-sign material as Moon oppressed by Saturn, or indeed Mercury, and announces the next twelve-sign descriptions for lunar affliction by Mars OR Sun. This retrospective/general extension remains separate from the marginal Saturn/Mars row labels and from sign-specific lunar prerequisites.'],
1690:['Moon in Aries afflicted by Mars conjunction, square OR opposition at first illness. Membranes/pellices of brain affected, continued fever, unrest, hot thirsty mouth, extreme thirst, dry tongue, hot/inflamed liver, breast heat, high/sublated irregular pulse; phrensy or deprivation of senses may be feared. Bloodletting and cooling/nourishing are described as helpful.','If NEXT after separation from Mars evil beams/aspect, the Moon also applies to Saturn conjunction OR opposition while DECREASING in light and SLOW in motion, there are small hopes of life and religious preparation is urged. This is not any Saturn contact or an unconditional death result.','First-person addition: usually near madness, or extreme belly/small-gut pain from colic obstruction.'],
1691:['Moon in Taurus afflicted by Mars conjunction/square/opposition at onset. Excess ill blood, continual fever, whole-body obstruction, throat/neck/hind-neck inflammation, bone ache, unkind slumbers without sleep, desire for wine/cold water. Bloodletting and moderately cooling/allaying heat are described as necessary.','First-person additions: strangury, stone/gravel in reins/kidneys, pestilent sore throats, hoarseness or malignity in that member.'],
1692:['Moon in Gemini afflicted by Mars at taking bed, with marginal conjunction/square/opposition. Usually violent dangerous fever, obstructions, high/inordinate pulse, overly hot/rank blood and body near corruption; blood emission is advocated historically.','First-person additions: pain throughout body with no settled location, extremely windy/corrupt/hot blood, lameness or grief in arms/joints, stone or heat in reins, and sometimes spitting blood. Exhaustion is not independently asserted in this row.'],
1693:['Moon in Cancer afflicted by Mars: abundant sweet phlegm in stomach, too much ingurgitation or surfeit, frequent vomiting or wish to vomit, with turning/eversion of the ventricle.','The first-person continuation calls it usually a mere surfeit from riot/excess and says most people the writer has seen thus afflicted were cured by vomiting. It many times turns to looseness or a rotten filthy cough, sometimes with spitting blood. The cure assertion has no number of patients or independently verified endpoint.'],
1694:['Moon in Leo afflicted by Mars: excessive blood/strong fevers, very weak pulses, raving/raging fits, disturbed brain, poor appetite, heaviness/drowsiness, heart disorders and consumption danger.','The source says USUALLY death ABOUT THE NINTH DAY AFTER FIRST FALLING SICK, IF OTHER HEAVENLY CONFIGURATIONS ACCORD. Usual, approximate, time origin and corroboration restriction are retained.','First-person additions: overheated blood, near raging madness, excessive choler, over-dried body, possible pleurisy, faintness/swooning or much-afflicted heart. The author particularly fears Moon-Mars CONJUNCTION OR OPPOSITION in this sign more than elsewhere; this comparison must not be generalized to every aspect.'],
1695:['Moon in Virgo afflicted by Mars: belly alteration/flux or miseriacks, small fevers, choler/melancholy, remiss pulse, ventricle eversion and food loathing. Death WITHIN THIRTY DAYS is asserted IF FORTUNES DO NOT ASSIST.','First-person additions: wind-colic, often weak legs or near ankles; the writer says never finding an illness easily removable under this onset configuration. This does not establish a quantified slow recovery or certain eventual recovery.'],
1696:['Moon in Libra afflicted by Mars: plenitude of blood, intense fevers, high pulse, sleeplessness/no natural rest and whole-body inflammation.','First-person additions: overheated blood and disordered diet/surfeit, often stone/gravel or great kidney heat. The PDF314 continuation calls clysters and gentle cooling best, notes widespread very violent burning fevers, and calls bloodletting good. These remain historical descriptions.'],
1697:['Moon in Scorpio afflicted by Mars: neither better nor worse, but grievous private-part infirmity; usually ulceration, small or French pox, measles if children, haemorrhoids/piles.','First-person passage adds head snuffling, grievous colds/rheums, scabs and skin eruptions. It infers French pox/gonorrhea/burning from looking wanton, then insinuates foul play or spouse fault when a modest person asks. These appearance/morality/culpability inferences are historical allegations, never evidence about an actual person.','The row calls the condition corrupt blood, recommends heating/comfort, and calls it usually scandalous. Its local heating prescription must not be replaced by the broad Mars-cooling recommendation.'],
1698:['Moon in Sagittarius afflicted by Mars: desperate illness attributed to surfeit/gluttony/repletion, high fevers, choleric passions, flux/laske and few/faint or slow/weak pulses.','If the sick escapes the SEVENTH DAY, or more properly the day when the Moon comes to a TRUE SQUARE OF HER FIRST-LYING-DOWN PLACE, there are hopes of recovery. Seven days and the geometrical event are not automatically identical, nor is either a guaranteed cure.','First-person additions: overheated blood after excessive exercise, extreme burning, sometimes pestilent fever with bloodletting twice/thrice, hand/foot gout, itch/eruptions, sore throat or sharp rheum offending eyes.'],
1699:['Moon in Capricorn afflicted by Mars: no perfect concoction, abundant choler, desire to vomit, absent appetite, sinew swelling/puffing, immediate belly flux, continual/returning fevers, breast inflammation, ulceration or choleric humour in hands/joints/fingers; remiss slow pulse. Obstructive/constringent medicines are called useful.','First-person additions: inclination to yellow jaundice, meagre countenance and extreme leanness, blood disaffected throughout body, very hard to cure even by the most learned; usually little blood or highly corrupt blood. Difficult cure is not proof that recovery occurs.'],
1700:['At onset Moon in Aquarius, SLOW in motion AND DECREASING in light, afflicted by Mars. Sharp/violent affections or vehement passions are alleged origins.','Any favourable planet casting its GOOD ASPECT to the Moon at her FIRST SQUARE TO HER OWN INITIAL PLACE OR at opposition to that initial zodiacal degree is said to give present remedy after TWENTY DAYS. Both the transit condition and the literal time phrase remain; this text alone does not reconcile their chronology or compute a cure date.','First-person additions, especially under opposition: heart pain, swooning, desperate fever, blood swelling veins, high pulses, sometimes breast pain and difficult breathing.'],
1701:['Moon in Pisces afflicted by Mars, INCREASING in light AND SWIFT in motion: full gross humours, excessive eating/swilling/drinking as alleged origin, worse disease at night, phrensy/delirium, sharp burning fever, vehement thirst and desire for wine.','First-person continuation PDF315–316: violent looseness, belly pain or extraordinary rotten cough, continual rheum from head into throat with near suffocation, swollen belly and dropsy danger. The two-page continuation is one row; not another case.'],
1702:['The upper PDF316 paragraph ends the Mars/Pisces continuation at danger of dropsy. The divider and following Astrologicall Aphorismes heading establish the next section. This editorial boundary record is not an additional substantive prognosis or patient.']}
for num,r in R.items():
 r['source_details']=DETAIL[num]
 r['source_statement_type']='normalized_paraphrase_not_diplomatic_transcription'
